      },
      "worked": "At each contact point, the curve has the stated value and the derivative equals the line's gradient. Since $y'=3ax^2+2bx+c$,\n$$\\begin{align*}8a+4b+2c+d&=9\\\\12a+4b+c&=18\\\\a+b+c+d&=0\\\\3a+2b+c&=3.\\end{align*}$$\nSubtracting the value equations gives $7a+3b+c=9$. Using $c=3-3a-2b$ gives $4a+b=6$. Subtracting the gradient equations gives $9a+2b=15$. Therefore\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=3\\\\b&=-6\\\\c&=6\\\\d&=-3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
